From 0dce1190fcb0262ed4059581867a92dafec3f234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc-moe <arc-moe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:19:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] sycl setup: native runner, CPU image encoder, every Arc
 in the layer split

- STRATA_SYCL_NATIVE (default when the strata-sycl-dev image is absent):
  serve/strata-sycl-native.sh sources oneAPI and runs the engine on the host;
  host paths in the config; the Arc switches in its "env" (device plan,
  NO_HOST=auto, stager threads, Sysman, relaxed >4 GB allocations, the
  device selector, the split's mirror pricing).
- Images: setup's CPU encoder build (tools/vision, #304) into engine-sycl/,
  and the config keeps its "vision" section; --vision cpu by default.
- Two or more Arcs: --gpus with all of them (layers split, auto).
- VRAM reserve 1536 MiB up to 32K.

The device selector "arc" is resolved by the runner to the discrete Arcs as
Level Zero numbers them, so an Intel CPU's integrated GPU never takes a
card's place in the split.
